IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g3-nouns`
IMPORT `g3-art8-register`
IMPORT `g3-art9-restricted-section`
IMPORT `g3-art10-public-access`
IMPORT `g3-fixtures`

-- g3-tests-readings.l4: each reading of each fork is a callable function (the R4 shape), and each is tested here DIRECTLY on its discriminating case, without the record.
-- The public decisions are tested with the record in the other test modules; the expected values below are decided from the reading's own definition in FRAGMENT-G3.md section 2.

§ `Each reading of each fork, called directly`

fav MEANS `the favoured interpretation of Articles 8 to 10`

`the 2019 constitution` MEANS
    `Copy held by the Commissioner (Article 8(6))` WITH
        kind IS `the constitution of the charity, or an amendment to it`
        `date received or made` IS YMD 2019 3 1
        `date it ceased to be operative` IS NOTHING

`the 2019 constitution, amended on 15 June 2021` MEANS
    `Copy held by the Commissioner (Article 8(6))` WITH
        kind IS `the constitution of the charity, or an amendment to it`
        `date received or made` IS YMD 2019 3 1
        `date it ceased to be operative` IS JUST (YMD 2021 6 15)

§§ `F3.1: when the ten years begin`

#ASSERT `F3.1 reading A: ten years from the day the copy is received or made` fav `the 2019 constitution` EQUALS `the copy may be discarded on and after` (YMD 2029 3 2)
#ASSERT `F3.1 reading B: ten years from the day the charity is deregistered` fav `Alpha, registered on 1 March 2019 and deregistered on 1 June 2024` EQUALS `the copy may be discarded on and after` (YMD 2034 6 2)
#ASSERT `F3.1 reading B: ten years from the day the charity is deregistered` fav `Alpha, registered on 1 March 2019` EQUALS `the copy is not to be discarded while the charity remains registered`
#ASSERT `F3.1 reading C: ten years from the day the copy ceases to be operative` fav `the 2019 constitution, amended on 15 June 2021` `Alpha, registered on 1 March 2019` EQUALS `the copy may be discarded on and after` (YMD 2031 6 16)
#ASSERT `F3.1 reading C: ten years from the day the copy ceases to be operative` fav `the 2019 constitution` `Alpha, registered on 1 March 2019` EQUALS `the copy is not to be discarded while the charity remains registered`

§§ `F3.2: what a year is`

`the financial year facts` MEANS
    `Facts for the annual return entry (Article 8(3)(j))` WITH
        `a date on which the charity's financial year ends` IS JUST (YMD 2026 6 30)
        `annual returns sent` IS EMPTY

`no financial year facts` MEANS
    `Facts for the annual return entry (Article 8(3)(j))` WITH
        `a date on which the charity's financial year ends` IS NOTHING
        `annual returns sent` IS EMPTY

#ASSERT `F3.2 reading A: the last day of the calendar year` 2026 EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 12 31)
#ASSERT `F3.2 reading B: the last day of the charity's own financial year` fav `the financial year facts` 2027 EQUALS JUST (YMD 2027 6 30)
#ASSERT `F3.2 reading B: the last day of the charity's own financial year` fav `no financial year facts` 2027 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `F3.2 reading C: the last day of the twelve months from an anniversary of registration` fav `Alpha, registered on 1 March 2019` 2026 EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 2 28)
#ASSERT `F3.2 reading C: the last day of the twelve months from an anniversary of registration` fav `Alpha, registered on 1 March 2019` 2024 EQUALS JUST (YMD 2024 2 29)

§§ `F3.3: does "registered charity" in Article 10(4) include a deregistered entity?`

#ASSERT NOT `F3.3 reading A: a registered charity is an entity entered in the general or the restricted section only` `formerly registered and entered in the historic section`
#ASSERT `F3.3 reading B: a registered charity includes an entity formerly registered and entered in the historic section` `formerly registered and entered in the historic section`
#ASSERT `F3.3 reading A: a registered charity is an entity entered in the general or the restricted section only` `entered in the restricted section`
#ASSERT `F3.3 reading B: a registered charity includes an entity formerly registered and entered in the historic section` `entered in the general section`
#ASSERT NOT `F3.3 reading B: a registered charity includes an entity formerly registered and entered in the historic section` `an applicant for registration`

§§ `F3.4 and F3.5: the tenth anniversary and the day after it`

#ASSERT `F3.4 reading A: the day of the event is not counted, so the last day of the period is the anniversary` fav (YMD 2019 3 1) 10 EQUALS YMD 2029 3 2
#ASSERT `F3.4 reading B: the day of the event is the first day, so the last day of the period is the day before the anniversary` fav (YMD 2019 3 1) 10 EQUALS YMD 2029 3 1
#ASSERT `F3.5 reading A: the date moves back to the last day of the month` (YMD 2016 2 29) 10 EQUALS YMD 2026 2 28
#ASSERT `F3.5 reading B: the date rolls forward into the next month` (YMD 2016 2 29) 10 EQUALS YMD 2026 3 1

§§ `F3.6: the day an entry takes effect`

`the placement of 1 June 2021` MEANS `a placement in` `the restricted section` `on` (YMD 2021 6 1)

#ASSERT `F3.6 reading A: an entry takes effect on the day of the entry` `the placement of 1 June 2021` (YMD 2021 6 1)
#ASSERT NOT `F3.6 reading A: an entry takes effect on the day of the entry` `the placement of 1 June 2021` (YMD 2021 5 31)
#ASSERT NOT `F3.6 reading B: an entry takes effect on the day after the entry` `the placement of 1 June 2021` (YMD 2021 6 1)
#ASSERT `F3.6 reading B: an entry takes effect on the day after the entry` `the placement of 1 June 2021` (YMD 2021 6 2)

§§ `F3.7: which year is the most recent`

`three year-ends` MEANS LIST (YMD 2025 12 31), (YMD 2026 12 31), (YMD 2027 12 31)

#ASSERT `F3.7 reading A: the latest year that has ended before the day asked` (YMD 2026 6 30) `three year-ends` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2025 12 31)
#ASSERT `F3.7 reading B: the year in progress on the day asked` (YMD 2026 6 30) `three year-ends` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 12 31)
#ASSERT `F3.7 reading A: the latest year that has ended before the day asked` (YMD 2026 12 31) `three year-ends` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2025 12 31)
#ASSERT `F3.7 reading B: the year in progress on the day asked` (YMD 2026 12 31) `three year-ends` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 12 31)
#ASSERT `F3.7 reading A: the latest year that has ended before the day asked` (YMD 2025 12 31) EMPTY EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `F3.8: which required steps notices are noted`

`a notice complied with` MEANS
    `Required steps notice` WITH
        `served on` IS `the registered charity`
        `prompted by` IS `there has been misconduct by a registered charity`
        `date served` IS YMD 2024 1 10
        `steps to be taken by` IS NOTHING
        `requires a governor to be suspended, removed or replaced` IS FALSE
        `has been complied with` IS TRUE

`a notice outstanding` MEANS
    `Required steps notice` WITH
        `served on` IS `a governor of the registered charity`
        `prompted by` IS `a governor of a registered charity has engaged in misconduct`
        `date served` IS YMD 2025 3 5
        `steps to be taken by` IS NOTHING
        `requires a governor to be suspended, removed or replaced` IS FALSE
        `has been complied with` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `F3.8 reading A: every notice that has been served` (LIST `a notice complied with`, `a notice outstanding`) EQUALS LIST `a notice complied with`, `a notice outstanding`
#ASSERT `F3.8 reading B: only a notice that has not been complied with` (LIST `a notice complied with`, `a notice outstanding`) EQUALS LIST `a notice outstanding`
#ASSERT `F3.8 reading B: only a notice that has not been complied with` (LIST `a notice complied with`) EQUALS EMPTY

§§ `F3.9 and F3.10: the principal address`

`a foundation whose Law requires nothing` MEANS
    `Facts for the principal address (Article 8(4))` WITH
        `its constitutional Law requires a registered office or business address in Jersey` IS FALSE
        `registered office or business address in Jersey` IS JUST "2 Bath Street"
        `main premises in Jersey from which its activities in Jersey are managed, controlled or undertaken` IS NOTHING
        `addresses in Jersey of the governors` IS LIST "3 Rue Bas"

#ASSERT NOT `F3.9 reading A: only an entity that its constitutional Law requires to have an office or address` (`an entity falling within` (LIST `a foundation`)) `a foundation whose Law requires nothing`
#ASSERT `F3.9 reading B: every company and foundation, and any other entity that its constitutional Law so requires` (`an entity falling within` (LIST `a foundation`)) `a foundation whose Law requires nothing`
#ASSERT `F3.10 reading A: Article 8(4)(b) does not apply to a private dwelling house, so Article 8(4)(c) is reached` `a foundation whose Law requires nothing` EQUALS LIST "3 Rue Bas"
#ASSERT `F3.10 reading B: Article 8(4)(b) applies to a private dwelling house and gives no address` `a foundation whose Law requires nothing` EQUALS EMPTY

§§ `F3.11: the section that decides Article 8(5)(b)`

`general then restricted` MEANS
    `Facts for the items of Article 8(5)` WITH
        `placements of the entity before deregistration` IS LIST (`a placement in` `the general section` `on` (YMD 2019 3 1)), (`a placement in` `the restricted section` `on` (YMD 2021 6 1))
        `previous registered names` IS EMPTY
        `matters prescribed by an Order under Article 8(5)(e)` IS EMPTY

#ASSERT NOT `F3.11 reading A: the section the entity was entered in immediately before deregistration` `general then restricted`
#ASSERT `F3.11 reading B: any section the entity was ever entered in` `general then restricted`

§§ `F3.12: who must meet a condition under Article 9(2)`

#ASSERT `F3.12 reading A: whoever makes the request, an applicant for registration or a registered charity` `a company in the general section` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `F3.12 reading B: only an applicant for registration` `a company in the general section` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `F3.12 reading B: only an applicant for registration` `a company that applies` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `F3.12 reading A: whoever makes the request, an applicant for registration or a registered charity` `a company in the restricted section` TRUE TRUE

§§ `F3.13: does Article 8(3)(a) reach sub-paragraph (ba)?`

#ASSERT NOT `sub-paragraph (ba) is treated like the sub-paragraphs the note names` fav
#ASSERT `sub-paragraph (ba) is treated like the sub-paragraphs the note names` `interpretation F3.13 reading B`
